      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Very slightly, there are times when bunnyhop (the technique of jumping while maintaining perfection) is possible.\nPersonally, I want an option to make bunny hop easier in the world (reducing the grace of continuous jumps or auto-hopping by holding it down), or to disable bunny hops at all.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2020-04-02T04:40:09.202Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "For SDK3 movement.\n\nJumping: When jumping and you connect with a ceiling, you stay floating in the air until it finishes applying the impulse, instead of starting falling. (You can test this easily with, say, an impulse 10 jump and a low obstacle overhead).\n\nJumping while Crouching: A player can air-strafe when jumping normally, however they cannot do this reliable when jumping from a crouching position.\n\nLanding: When you are about to hit the ground you stop completely for a second... then slowly sink to the correct spot on the floor.\n\nMaybe a little lower priority, but this, like stutter stepping / wall climbing, continues to give movement in VRChat a somewhat 'unpolished' feel.",
